{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz","lean:module:QOU.ComputationalHorizon","lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.q_bkm_criterion"],"declarations":32,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.regular_iff_bkm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.regular_iff_bkm","kind":"theorem","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L376-L388","doc":"**The corpus q-BKM criterion is the bridge's regularity dichotomy.** Given a\n`QBKMContext` whose `extendsSmoothly` / `vorticityIntegralFinite` predicates\nare modelled by the bridge's *no blow-up* / *bounded filtration* predicates,\nthe q-BKM iff (`QOU.FluidDynamics.q_bkm_criterion`) transports to\n`noBlowUp ↔ boundedFiltration` — i.e. q-NS smoothness **is** the filtration-\nboundedness question the bridge poses. The two modelling hypotheses are\nexplicit; nothing is assumed silently. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.vortexReductionSystem_regular_and_halts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.vortexReductionSystem_regular_and_halts","kind":"theorem","line":357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L357-L374","doc":"**The shared descent exists on the concrete vortex flow.** Firing\n`regular_and_halts_of_len_orbit_descent` on `vortexReductionSystem`: its\ncrossing-count reduction is a genuine controlled descent, so it yields q-NS\nregularity **and** q-Collatz-style halting from the single hypothesis — a\nconcrete, unconditional witness that the shared-descent machinery is\nnon-vacuous. (The real q-Collatz descent measure `μ` on `ℤ[q^{±1}]` remains\nthe open wall — it is *not* constructed here, only exhibited on this toy\nreduction.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.vortexReductionSystem_halts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.vortexReductionSystem_halts","kind":"theorem","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L349-L355","doc":"The crossing-reduction flow **halts** — every knot resolves to the unknot `0`\n(the complexity strictly descends off `0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.vortexReductionSystem_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.vortexReductionSystem_regular","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L339-L347","doc":"The crossing-reduction flow is **regular** — its complexity is non-increasing,\nso it never blows up (bound = the initial crossing number). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.vortexReductionSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.vortexReductionSystem","kind":"def","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L331-L337","doc":"A concrete vortex flow: crossing-count `n : ℕ`, one crossing resolved per step\n(`n ↦ n − 1`), observation = the complexity, normal form = the unknot `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.horizon_numLeaves_eq_three_pow_filtrationLevel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.horizon_numLeaves_eq_three_pow_filtrationLevel","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L314-L318","doc":"The resolution-tree leaf count is `3` to the filtration level — the naive,\nexponential observation cost the P side must beat. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.horizonFiltrationLevel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.horizonFiltrationLevel","kind":"def","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L307-L312","doc":"The horizon's **crossing count** `c` is the natural filtration level: `N`\nToffoli gates give `c = 3N` crossings and a resolution tree with `3^c`\nleaves, so the brute-force observation cost is exponential in the filtration.\nP-vs-NP asks whether the degree-0 observation is `PolyObservable` with a\nbudget sub-exponential in this level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qCollatzSystem_haltsObserved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qCollatzSystem_haltsObserved","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L297-L303","doc":"The bridge recovers `reaches_cycle_observed`: conditional on the conjecture\n(`QCollatz.reaches_cycle`), a positive q-Collatz orbit's observed output\nstabilises to the attractor's — observed halting to the unknot trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qCollatzSystem_halts_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qCollatzSystem_halts_iff","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L289-L295","doc":"q-Collatz `reaches_cycle` **is** `Halts` in the bridge — the two problems are\nthe same reachability question in this abstraction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qCollatzSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qCollatzSystem","kind":"def","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L276-L287","doc":"The **q-Collatz halting problem** as a Skein-observation system: `step = C_q`,\n`obs` a chosen observation map (the Markov trace into `V`), `normalForm` the\nfundamental 2-cycle attractor, and `len` the intended `[2]_q`-adic descent\nmeasure (any ℕ-measure typechecks; the valuation is the intended witness).\nConditional on a `[QCollatz Skein]` instance — no fabricated data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.separation_of_residue_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.separation_of_residue_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L252-L272","doc":"**The lift-and-contradict skeleton.** Suppose the framework's central\nequivalence holds — the P=NP horizon collapse is EQUIVALENT to the vanishing\nof the obstruction residue (`hequiv : PolyCollapse ↔ resZero`) — and the\nresidue is provably non-zero (`hres : ¬ resZero`, a topological computation\nof `χ(A)`). Then the collapse cannot occur (`¬ PolyCollapse`): the\nseparation.\n\nContrapositive reading — exactly the user's \"lift an example P=NP and\ncontradict\": *if* the collapse held, *then* (through the equivalence) the\nresidue would vanish, contradicting `hres`.\n\n**Both hypotheses are open inputs.** `hequiv` is the faithfulness leg\n(`QOU.Information.PNeqNpEquivalence`, still `sorry`); `hres` is the χ(A)\nnon-vanishing. This is a modus-tollens *by design* — the machine-checked\nSHAPE of the argument, proving nothing about P vs NP unconditionally, and it\ndoes NOT by itself clear the algebrization barrier (the residue must be a\ngenuinely non-algebraic cohomological invariant for the argument to have\ncontent). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_polyObservable_id_of_horizon_cost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_polyObservable_id_of_horizon_cost","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L238-L246","doc":"**Concrete separation.** A system with exponential horizon cost is not\npoly-observable under the identity (linear) budget — `lt_three_pow` discharges\nthe gap unconditionally, so the exponential lower bound alone yields the\nseparation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_polyObservable_of_horizon_cost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_polyObservable_of_horizon_cost","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L224-L236","doc":"**Exponential horizon cost ⇒ not poly-observable.** If every observation-match\nhappens no earlier than the resolution-tree cost `3^{len P}` (`hcost`), then no\npolynomial budget the horizon exceeds (`poly (len P) < 3^{len P}`) suffices —\nthe P-vs-NP separation, with the exponential lower bound `hcost` taken as the\n(genuinely hard) hypothesis rather than proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.regular_and_halts_of_len_orbit_descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.regular_and_halts_of_len_orbit_descent","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L194-L212","doc":"**One descent, two walls.** A globally non-increasing filtration that\nadditionally drops strictly off the normal form gives **both** q-NS\nregularity (bounded by the initial complexity) **and** q-Collatz halting.\nThe two open walls share one missing ingredient — a controlled descent on\nthe Skein filtration; P-vs-NP is the same descent with the *polynomial-rate*\nrefinement added. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.regular_of_len_nonincreasing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.regular_of_len_nonincreasing","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L171-L183","doc":"**Non-increasing filtration ⇒ regularity** (bound = initial complexity). The\nabstract shadow of q-BKM: a monotone Lyapunov filtration (bounded / decaying\nenstrophy — the vortex-knot complexity never grows) rules out finite-time\nblow-up. The same monotonicity that drives q-Collatz descent gives q-NS\nregularity; only P-vs-NP additionally demands the descent be *polynomially\nfast*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_blowsUp_of_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_blowsUp_of_regular","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L164-L169","doc":"A regular orbit does not blow up. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.BlowsUp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.BlowsUp","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L160-L162","doc":"**Blow-up**: the filtration is unbounded along the orbit — the finite-time\nsingularity of a q-NS solution (negation of regularity for every bound). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.Regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.Regular","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L155-L158","doc":"**Regularity / no finite-time blow-up** (q-NS): the length filtration stays\nbounded by `B` along the whole orbit — the vortex-knot complexity never\ndiverges. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.PolyCollapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.PolyCollapse","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L137-L142","doc":"**P=NP collapse** at the level of one distinguished `universal` state: it is\npoly-observable within the budget. This is the object a hypothetical P=NP\nwould furnish; the separation lemma below shows it cannot exist under the\nresidue-non-vanishing hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.haltsObserved_of_polyObservable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.haltsObserved_of_polyObservable","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L131-L135","doc":"Poly-observability refines observed halting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.PolyObservable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.PolyObservable","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L122-L129","doc":"**Poly-observability** — the \"P\" side. Given a length budget `poly`, an\nelement is poly-observable if its observed output is reached within\n`poly (len P)` steps: *polynomially* in the filtration level, not the naive\n`3^c` leaf count of the resolution tree (`ComputationalHorizon.numLeaves`).\nThis is the bridge form of the P-vs-NP horizon question. Left as an OPEN\npredicate — nothing here proves it holds or fails. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.halts_of_len_descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.halts_of_len_descent","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L111-L120","doc":"**Descent ⇒ halting**, over a forward-invariant cone graded by `len`.\nAbstract form of `reaches_of_descent_of_forward`: if `len` strictly\ndecreases off the normal form on a forward-invariant cone `C`, every element\nof `C` halts. The *open* content of both q-Collatz and P-vs-NP is precisely\nthe existence of such a descent for their filtration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.haltsObserved_of_halts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.haltsObserved_of_halts","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L102-L109","doc":"**The general C12**: halting implies observed halting. The observation is a\nfunctorial shadow of the dynamics — the abstract form of\n`reaches_cycle_observed`. The converse is false in general (distinct states\ncan share a Skein value), which is exactly why the observable is *easy* and\nthe halting is *hard*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.HaltsObserved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.HaltsObserved","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L96-L100","doc":"**Observed halting**: the observed output reaches the normal form's. This is\nthe *decidable shadow* — it depends only on the Markov trace, not the full\ndynamics. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.Halts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.Halts","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L93-L94","doc":"**Halting**: the orbit reaches the normal form (the dynamical question). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.len","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.len","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L87-L87","doc":"The ℕ-valued length/complexity filtration grading the reduction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.normalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.normalForm","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L85-L85","doc":"The normal-form target — the fundamental cycle / the unknot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.obs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.obs","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The observation map: the Markov trace / Jones value the observer reads. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.step","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L81-L81","doc":"One reduction step of the dynamical system (`C_q`; one crossing resolution). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.mk","kind":"ctor","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem","kind":"structure","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L73-L87","doc":"An abstract **Skein-observation system**: a discrete dynamical system on a\nstate space `S`, with an observation map `obs : S → V` (the Markov trace), a\nnormal-form target (the attractor / unknot), and a ℕ-valued length /\ncomplexity filtration `len` (crossing count / braid length / `[2]_q`-adic\nvaluation). Both the q-Collatz halting problem and the P-vs-NP computational\nhorizon are instances. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.lt_three_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.lt_three_pow","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinObservationBridge.lean#L61-L71","doc":"The resolution-tree horizon `3^n` exceeds its input `n` for every `n`, so a\nlinear observation budget never reaches the exponential cost. (The exponential\n`3^n` in fact dominates every polynomial eventually; `n < 3^n` is the piece the\nlinear-budget corollary needs.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}